:: Arcology Stack Bunk
<<effects>>
You find an empty bunk and climb onto the thin foam mat. The mat is so narrow that your elbows touch the sides of the frame when you lie down. You adjust the mat beneath your shoulders and try to get comfortable.
<br><br>
You can still hear the conveyors working on the other side of the wall. When a heavier load passes through the machinery, the metal bed frame moves slightly. You turn onto your side and try to sleep while the workers around you settle into their own bunks.
<br><br>
<<nightmareCheck "Arcology Stack Sleep">>
<<generateSleepLinks "Arcology Stack Sleep">>
<<link [[Climb off the bunk|Arcology Stack Bunks]]>><<loadTempHairStyle>><</link>>
<br><br>

:: Arcology Stack Sleep
<<set _autosavehere to true>>
<<sleep false `(30 - Time.hour) % 24`>><<effects>><<wakingEffects $sleepHoursTotal>>
<<if ["dryheaving","nausea"].includes(_wakingEffect)>>
	<br><br>
	You open your eyes and sit up slowly. Your stomach feels unsettled, and you stay on the edge of the bunk until you feel ready to stand.
	<br><br>
<<elseif $nightmares gte 1 and $controlled is 0>>
	<<nightmareWake>>
<<elseif !_wakingEffect>>
	You wake after several hours of sleep. The lights over the bunks are still on, and other workers are beginning to move around the sleeping area.
	<br><br>
<<else>>
	<br><br>
<</if>>
<<sleepeffects>>
<<if Time.hour gte 6 and Time.hour lt 21>>
	A drone enters the sleeping area and moves slowly between the rows of bunks. Its bright light passes across your bed, making you cover your eyes. A horn announces the next shift, and workers begin climbing down the ladders to put on their shoes and head towards the sorting room.
	<br><br>
<</if>>
<<link [[Next|Arcology Stack Bunks]]>><</link>>
<br>

