:: Arcology Stack Release
<<pass 5>><<effects>>
<<badEndTrackingEnd "Arcology Stack" { reason: "arcologyStackPaid" }>>
You hold your ankle band where the supervisor can read it. The display shows zero beside your handle, with no new charges beneath it.
<br><br>
The supervisor checks the balance against a handheld reader, then tells you to hold your foot still. The supervisor removes the metal band and places it in a box containing bands from other workers.
<br><br>
"Your debt's paid," the supervisor says. "You can leave."
<br><br>
A worker carrying a bin stops to watch the supervisor put the band away. "You actually paid it off?" the worker asks. You show your bare ankle, and the worker smiles. "Get going before they find something else to charge you for."
<br><br>
You walk past the conveyors towards the service lift. At the doors, a scanner checks the implant behind your ear. A green light appears on the panel, and the doors open. Nobody stops you from entering.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Arcology Stack Release 2]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Stack Release 2
<<pass 5>><<effects>>
You step into the lift and press the button for the pier. The doors close, and the lift begins taking you back towards the upper levels of the city.
<br><br>
During the journey, the warning beside your implant status changes from red to green. You open the message to read the new information.
<br><br>
<<holo "CIVIC REGISTRY / STATUS CHANGE" "ok">>
	<<holoRow "HANDLE" `$xchange.arcology.handle`>>
	<<holoRow "STATUS" "RELEASED">>
	<<holoLine "BALANCE CLEARED" "ok">>
<</holo>>
<br>
The lift stops beneath the white pier, and its doors open onto a passage leading outside. You walk past the service entrance and reach the pier without a guard following you.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Arcology Pier]]>><<arcologyStackEnd>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Stack Rescue
<<effects>>
<<set $xchange.arcology.stack.rescue to "offered">>
<<npc Luchifen>><<person1>>
<<LuName>> steps out of the service lift wearing a long black coat. A supervisor approaches to question the visitor, then recognises <<luName>> and puts the tablet away.
<br><br>
<<LuName>> speaks briefly to the supervisor, then walks between the sorting stations until they reach you. The workers nearby continue sorting, although several turn to see why someone from the upper city has come down here.
<br><br>
They stop beside your station and look you over, pausing at the band on your ankle. You turn it so they can read the balance.
<br><br>
"I was beginning to wonder where you had gone," they say. "I asked at the checkpoint. Apparently, this is where my guest has been staying." They glance towards the supervisor, who suddenly finds something to check on the tablet. "I can settle that balance. Then we can find you somewhere rather more comfortable."
<br><br>
They hold out a hand. "Will you come with me?"
<br><br>
<<link [[Go with them|Arcology Stack Rescue Go]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Tell them you'll pay it yourself|Arcology Stack Rescue Stay]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Stack Rescue Go
<<pass 5>><<effects>>
<<badEndTrackingEnd "Arcology Stack" { reason: "arcologyStackRescued" }>>
You take <<luName>>'s hand. They ask the supervisor to charge the balance to their account and wait while the payment goes through. Once the reader confirms it, the supervisor cuts the band from your ankle.
<br><br>
<<LuName>> leads you towards the lift while the supervisor steps aside. Once you are both inside and the doors close, <<luName>> releases your hand and turns to face you.
<br><br>
"When I said you were my guest, I had something rather different in mind," they say. You look down at your ankle, where the band has left a mark. They look at the mark too and pause before continuing.
<br><br>
"If you find yourself in trouble again, do try to tell me before the guards put you to work. I would prefer to hear it from you rather than a clerk." <<npcincr Luchifen love -10>><<llllove>>
<br><br>
<<holo "CIVIC REGISTRY / STATUS CHANGE" "ok">>
	<<holoRow "HANDLE" `$xchange.arcology.handle`>>
	<<holoRow "STATUS" "RELEASED">>
	<<holoLine "BALANCE CLEARED" "ok">>
<</holo>>
<br>
The lift doors open beneath the white pier. You follow <<luName>> out through the staff passage. At the public walkway, they wait while you catch your breath, then point out the way back to the city before continuing along the pier.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Arcology Pier]]>><<arcologyStackEnd>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Stack Rescue Stay
<<pass 5>><<effects>>
<<set $xchange.arcology.stack.rescue to "refused">>
<<LuName>> keeps their hand out while you explain why you want to stay. The workers nearby continue sorting, trying to listen without turning towards you.
<br><br>
<<speechresolve>><<switch _speechAttitudeResolved>>
<<case "meek">>
	"Thank you, but... I think I should pay it myself," you say quietly.
<<case "shy">>
	"I appreciate it," you say, struggling to look at them. "I want to finish paying it myself."
<<case "polite">>
	"Thank you for coming here, but I'd prefer to finish paying my debt myself," you say.
<<case "confident">>
	"I can pay my own debt," you say. "I'm staying until it's cleared."
<<case "bratty">>
	"I can get out of here without you paying for me," you say. "Just watch."
<<case "docile">>
	"I'd like to stay and pay the debt myself, if that's all right," you say softly.
<<case "flamboyant">>
	"It's a generous offer," you say. "But I'd rather walk out of here knowing I paid every Cipher myself."
<<case "cruel">>
	"Keep your money," you say. "I don't need you to pay my way out."
<<default>>
	"Thanks for coming," you say. "But I'm going to pay the debt myself."
<</switch>>
<br><br>
They lower their hand and look at the balance once more. "You would rather work until you have paid all of that?" You confirm it, and they step back from your station. "Very well. I will leave you to it. Though I hope you know what the Stack charges for the privilege of sleeping here."
<br><br>
<<LuName>> turns towards the lift. The supervisor waits beside the doors for <<luName>> to step inside, then orders everyone to return to work once the doors close.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Arcology Stack]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Arcology Stack Birth
<<effects>>
<<if !$xchange.arcology.stack.medic>>
	<<set $xchange.arcology.stack.medic to true>>
	<<arcologyNPC 1 "worker" "medic">><<saveNPC 1 "stack_medic">><<person2>>
	Two workers bring you to a cot in the medical area. You lie on your side while two people argue nearby. You can make out a worker's voice, followed by a guard's.
	<br><br>
	"I usually treat cuts and burns," the worker says. "I've never had to deliver a baby down here."
	<br><br>
	"There's nobody else coming," the guard replies. "Help with the birth."
<<else>>
	<<loadNPC 1 "stack_medic">><<person2>>
	The workers help you onto the medical cot. Someone moves a lamp above you, and you recognise the medic's voice.
	<br><br>
	"Another delivery," the medic says. "Somebody hold the lamp where I can see."
<</if>>
<br><br>
You turn towards the bright lamp above the medical cot. The Stack's medic is standing beside you, preparing an injector. A guard is standing a short distance from the cot, watching as the medic checks your condition.
<br><br>
"I'm giving you something for the pain," the <<person>> says, pressing the injector against your arm. "When I tell you to push, do your best. I'll tell you what's happening."
<br><br>
You try to adjust your position on the cot. The medic helps you lie back and moves the lamp so <<he>> can see what <<he>> is doing.
<br><br>
<<wash>><<undress "stack_birth">>
